; The walking bass's players: how the bassist behind each soloist walks, measured in the Weimar
; Jazz Database v2.1 (the bass's pitch on each beat under its swing solos, 4/4; mostly
; automatic estimates, so the rows are read against the whole database's, not as absolutes).
; Statistics only: the walker makes its own lines from them (`src/audio/live/walkers.rs`).
;
; `slug = Name | steps .. | lands .. | approach .. | inside .. | pedal ..`, in % of beats:
;   steps     beat to beat: the same note, a half step, a whole step, a 3rd, a 4th or 5th, wider
;   lands     on a chord change: the root, the 3rd, the 5th, another note
;   approach  the beat before a change, against the next chord: a half step below its root, a
;             half step above, a whole step, its 5th, the same note again, another note
;   inside    within a chord: chord tones, scale tones, chromatic notes
;   pedal     beats in a pedal point (four or more on one pitch class)
;   push      the beat before a change already on the new root (an anticipation)
;   hold      the change's beat still on the note before (a suspension)
;   two       bars in two (half notes)
; and, where a note-level pass on the bassist's records measured them (optional):
;   skip      beats with a skip note at a medium tempo (fewer when fast), then where in the
;             beat it falls (0.66: on the triplet); unmeasured, 12% on the tune's swung 8th
;   rake      beats raked in triplets
;   ghost     notes ghosted (muted)
;   pair      bars of paired quarters (a two-feel struck in four: 1=2, 3=4), bars paired half

; The whole database (99567 beats under 346 solos): the band's own line walks like this.
all = The whole database | steps 20.3 22.2 13.5 14.1 18.4 11.5 | lands 41 11 11 37 | approach 14 14 17 15 7 34 | inside 51 19 30 | pedal 7.6 | push 6.6 | hold 12.1 | two 9.1
; Miles' 50s quintet, Coltrane's and Rollins' 50s dates: smooth and chromatic, hardly repeats.
; His rhythm from his separated bass on Relaxin' and Red Garland's Piano (12685 beats): a skip
; on the triplet every bar and a half, mostly before a change; ghosts (up to 18%, with bleed).
