; Dizzy's Sonny Side Up (1957), "On the Sunny Side of the Street": a note-level pass on his
; separated bass (a YouTube rip, Veesh's study copy; 120 bpm). A two-feel struck in four: paired
; quarters in a third of the bars (most in the bridges), all four even and detached, one note a
; bar or root to 4th/5th; out of it by a swung skip late in 4; hardly anticipates. The rest walks
; (pitch steps not measured: the database's), on Sunny Side (`bassist = bryant`).
